# A VALUE KNOWN AT COMPILE TIME MUST FIT THE DESTINATION IT LANDS IN, at a
# return and a reassignment as at an argument: `return 300` from an `out u8`
# printed 44 and `a = 0 - 5` into a u8 printed 251.
big: function out u8 is {
    return 300
}

main: function is {
    a: 1.u8
    a = 0 - 5
    print "\{a} \{big}"
}
